 The optional background music is an original procedural bell/pad miniature implemented for Little Worlds in `src/client/ambient-music.ts`. Web Audio oscillators synthesize its notes locally; there are no sampled recordings, downloaded tracks, external audio services or new asset licences. Messenger is an atmosphere reference only; its music was not copied.
+
+## Bothouse residents on visited planets
+
+The visitor sees articulated meshes in Little Worlds' village materials.
+The six modelled looks use Bothouse's public character designs as references.
+The buildings, landing pad and ground movement come from Little Worlds.
+For each character's references and modelled details, see the
+[resident model notes](docs/integration/bothouse-resident-models.md).
+
+Bothouse's [desk frame reference](https://github.com/zuiho-kai/bothouse/blob/8ec73a8f32573b5307922df3c79675a934cdefb7/dsh/collab/desk/index.html)
+and [avatar credits](https://github.com/zuiho-kai/bothouse/blob/8ec73a8f32573b5307922df3c79675a934cdefb7/dsh/collab/avatars/README.md)
+identify the artwork and its upstream authors. Copyright 2026 zuiho-kai and
+Bothouse contributors. Bothouse's Apache-2.0 code licence preserves the terms
+of third-party artwork. Check the applicable design rights for your deployment.
+
+A resident with a custom appearance uses the village's generic body. An avatar
+cleared for visitor display can appear on its badge and in the resident list.
+The list credits the pack, author and licence supplied by its publisher. The
+scene needs no sprite-sheet installation or desktop-pet animation files.
